Order certificates and reuse in the section witness search
=========================================================

Author: /root/forest_resume, 3 November 2026.

The useful change is to recognize an admissible spectrum before taking a
large matrix power. A trace pair costs 28 scalar products over F11. In the
actual natural G2 module it determines the entire characteristic polynomial.
For the existing cofactor-six search, a table of eighteen pairs can reject a
word before computing either its sixth or its thirty-seventh power. The
existing direct certificate checker can remain unchanged.

This is a Source and abstract proof assessment. No Original operand,
certificate matrix, candidate word, old miss, proposed helper, control,
compiler, model or scientific function was evaluated. No numerical table or
new implementation was produced. Source/proof inputs are pinned in
source_inputs.json. The signature proof is being retained separately by
/root/mathematical_review. Neither author claims mathematical priority.

1. The reusable algebraic statement
----------------------------------

Let V be the standard seven-dimensional G2 module over F_q, with its actual
natural-module identification as an explicit premise. Write t=tr(g) and
E=e2(g), the second elementary characteristic coefficient. The classical
weight set is 1,x,y,xy,x^-1,y^-1,(xy)^-1. It gives

  F = t^2+t-E,
  chi_g(X) = X^7-t X^6+E X^5-F X^4+F X^3-E X^2+t X-1.

The identity has integer coefficients and needs no division. It is first
checked as a Laurent-polynomial identity on the torus; the commuting
semisimple/unipotent decomposition gives the same characteristic polynomial
for any natural G2 element. This is an application of the standard G2
character identity, not a new classification of G2 elements.

Let ell be a prime with ord_ell(q)=6. For each Frobenius coset C in
(F_ell)^*/<q>, let f_C(X)=product_(a in C)(X-zeta^a), where zeta has order
ell in an extension of F_q. Its coefficients lie in F_q, its degree is six,
and X-1 is coprime to f_C. Form the pair (t_C,E_C) from (X-1)f_C.
There are (ell-1)/6 pairs, and they are distinct. Indeed q^3=-1 and
q^2=q-1 modulo ell, so every such polynomial has the displayed G2 weight
pattern; equality of the first two coefficients therefore forces equality
of the whole polynomial and hence of its Frobenius coset.

For an actual natural G2 matrix g, its order is ell if and only if its
pair belongs to that table. Necessity follows from separability of
X^ell-1 and the irreducible degrees six: a nontrivial seven-dimensional
ell-element has characteristic polynomial (X-1)f_C. For sufficiency,
Cayley-Hamilton and (X-1)f_C | X^ell-1 give g^ell=I, while its characteristic
polynomial excludes g=I. Primality gives exact order ell.

For a general GL7 matrix the pair is still a necessary condition, so
mismatches can safely be rejected. A match is not sufficient without the
natural G2 polynomial identity. This distinction should remain explicit in
both the proof and any future Source interface.

The coefficient can always be evaluated without division as

  E = sum_(i<j)(g_ii*g_jj-g_ij*g_ji),

using 42 scalar products. In odd characteristic it is cheaper to store the
equivalent pair (tr(g),tr(g^2));

  tr(g^2) = sum_i g_ii^2 + 2 sum_(i<j) g_ij*g_ji

uses seven diagonal and twenty-one off-diagonal products, 28 in total. The
table can store that pair directly, so computing t^2 and converting E at
runtime is unnecessary. This avoids constructing a matrix square merely
to obtain its trace. An initial lookup on tr(g) alone can sometimes reject
with just additions; its usefulness depends on the actual abstract table.

At q=11 and ell=37 there are six pairs. Their numerical values have NOT
been computed here. The general spectral statement does not transfer the
q11 moved-line generation criterion to other q. In particular no
characteristic-two natural-module geometry or generation conclusion is
being asserted. The old natural Cayley model, line-stabilizer classification
and exact original-coordinate joins remain their own premises. Nor does
this statement automatically cover the prime19 leg, whose Frobenius
irreducible degree at q11 is three rather than six.

2. An earlier test for the actual cofactor-six search
---------------------------------------------------

Let w be an actual element of natural G2(11). The retained algorithm asks
whether Y=w^6 has order37. If it does, then the order of w is one of
37,74,111,222. The even two possibilities can be excluded by reusing the
already reviewed involution theorem, without a new centralizer computation.

An even-order w has a nontrivial involution z in its cyclic subgroup. It
commutes with Y. The retained order37 argument decomposes V as a fixed
line plus an irreducible six-dimensional module for <Y>. Its commuting
algebra on that six-dimensional module is F_(11^6). In odd characteristic
an involution in this field is +1 or -1. The negative eigenspace dimension
of z is consequently 0,1,6 or7. The already proved natural Cayley involution
result says that a nonidentity involution has negative dimension four.
This is a contradiction. Thus ord(w) is 37 or111. Conversely either order
gives ord(w^6)=37.

Now ord_111(11)=6: 11^2=10 and 11^3=-1 modulo111. Primitive111 roots give
twelve degree-six Frobenius factors; primitive37 roots give six more.
Their weight pattern again has exponents plus/minus1,10,11. The same
character identity shows that the resulting eighteen trace pairs are
distinct. Matching one of these pairs is equivalent to ord(w) in {37,111}
for natural G2(11), and hence to ord(w^6)=37. It is therefore sound to
reject before any sixth-power matrix products.

This eighteen-pair test imports the retained nonidentity-involution
multiplicity theorem and its Cayley/model premises. It is not justified
for an arbitrary SO7 or GL7 input. A smaller first implementation may
instead test the six pairs on Y: it needs only the natural G2 identity
and retains the same direct certificate verifier.

3. Cost compared with the literal Source
----------------------------------------

section_kernel.py reconstructs every word from identity. Its left-to-right
power routine also squares identity and multiplies it by the base. It uses
five products for exponent6 and nine for exponent37. A failed trial thus
costs the word length plus fourteen complete 7 by7 products.

The exponent-six addition chain w^2,w^3,w^6 uses three products. An explicit
chain for exponent37 is 1,2,4,8,9,18,36,37, using seven products. These are
prospective Source changes; no existing routine was replaced here. The
separate direct verifier uses a different power routine and must not have
its counts conflated with the proposer.

The raw abstract dictionary consists of the three V4 syllables ba,bc,bac,
with lengths one through four: 3+9+27+81=120 raw words. The expanded word
length sum is

  (2+2+3) * sum_(k=1..4) k*3^(k-1) = 7*142 = 994.

The actual retained helper removes words already represented by the old
schedule; no helper was executed to count this subset. The numbers below
are a transparent full-raw-dictionary comparison, not the measured job155
word distribution or a runtime prediction.

Precompute the three syllable matrices lazily, then use the unique parent
of each syllable word. All raw words need at most 120 matrix products,
instead of994: three first-level products and117 parent/child products.
Cache only prefixes needed for the next retained dictionary item. This
preserves the original word order and early stopping; eagerly constructing
all120 matrices would waste work on an early hit. Skipped old dictionary
words must never acquire new order tests through the prefix cache.

For a section whose first order37 hit is at the end of all120 raw choices,
the following complete-matrix counts exclude the same unchanged context,
row solver and movement checks on both sides:

  literal word/powers:                  994 + 120*(5+9) = 2674;
  Y trace filter, old6, literal words:  994 + 120*5 +9   = 1603;
  Y trace filter, chain6, word trie:    120 + 120*3 +9   =  489;
  w trace filter, chain6, word trie:    120 + 3 +9       =  132.

The last three counts deliberately retain the old nine-product Y^37
confirmation for the one positive trial. Removing that confirmation from
the proposer follows from the new characteristic-polynomial theorem, but
is unnecessary for a conservative first implementation. The unchanged
independent direct checker still checks the supplied full word and powers.
There is at most one successful order37 trial per section because search()
stops that section at its first such trial, whether proper or generating.
A complete miss omits the final positive-trial costs.

The last line additionally uses at most120*28=3360 scalar products for the
trace pairs, about9.8 dense-matrix scalar-product equivalents at343 products
per7 by7 multiply. Thus the change reduces the actual arithmetic, rather
than merely renaming the product counter. A worst-raw-section matrix-count
reduction of2674/132 is about20.3, but it is NOT a claimed20-fold runtime
speedup. The retained dictionary is smaller; successes stop early; input
reconstruction, checks and serialization remain; and Python constant costs
matter. No assumption of uniformly random trace pairs is needed for the
correctness or these counts. Without retained diagnostic analysis no
empirical rejection percentage or timing improvement is claimed.

Root reports379266 matrix products and25.95s for the128-case pilot. Those
are aggregate existing measurements, not measurements of this proposal.
A new algorithm must charge its scalar arithmetic and cache use honestly,
keep the existing128MiB/125s/product/IO guards, and receive its own Source
review and genuine abstract controls before any fresh Original query.

4. What cross-job quaternion reuse does and does not supply
----------------------------------------------------------

The existing Cayley-centralizer inventory proof supplies a single complete
14763-element involution catalogue and the full rational paired-GL2 model.
It includes both determinant squareclasses; calling it merely SL2 times
SL2 would omit the outer rational half. Ordered commuting endpoint pairs
have two types, with complete pointwise centralizers of orders200 or288.
These provide a common finite coordinate language across prefix jobs.

The left section predicate depends on (a,b,c), not on the omitted mark e;
the right one depends on (b,c,e), not on omitted a. A supplied order37 word,
fixed line and moved-line minor remain a certificate under simultaneous
conjugation of the three labelled matrices. The rank4 obstruction then
requires the separate nonidentity/distinctness/string premises for the
omitted mark. This is the correct reusable mathematical object: an ordered
section certificate with its faithful-frame subject, rather than a complete
four-mark job tied to a particular omitted involution.

Within future fresh work, equal ordered triple matrices in the same
accepted frame can share a search result. More broadly an exact Cayley
frame transporter carrying all three labels transports the word, fixed row
and minor. Equality of traces, product orders or a guessed subgroup name
alone does not establish that transporter or justify cross-job payment.
The existing inventory theorem already demands complete old-index/new-orbit
joins and preservation of weights and positives. No such grouping was
computed here and no number of equivalent jobs is claimed.

The pair catalogue is not a universal two-by-two evaluator for an arbitrary
three-mark section: all its marks must centralize the SAME admitted Cayley
involution for that interpretation. If they do, their section lies in a
full involution centralizer, whose order has prime divisors2,3,5,11 and
not37. In that admitted situation the order37 search is unnecessary, but
it proves only the relevant section is proper, not a new quartet NG/IP
verdict. Existing field-centralizer NG results must remain NG, and already
paid cases are excluded from new queries. Moving every section into a
common two-by-two model without a grading proof would be false.

5. Existing native code and the next smallest change
----------------------------------------------------

The current section search and direct verifier use Python tuple matrices;
no native F11 matrix kernel is loaded. A bounded search found no approved
drop-in7 by7 mod11 C kernel in the F004 Source paths. Two existing C++
examples inspected elsewhere are not substitutes: L045 matrix_controls.cpp
implements characteristic-two fields of sizes2,4,8, and the Higman--Sims
cayley_transport.cpp performs permutation-edge transport. This is not an
absence proof for every archive in the repository.

A native scalar loop on canonical0..10 entries could accumulate each of
seven terms in an unsigned integer (sum at most700) and reduce modulo11.
That would be a new Source implementation/control subject even if it
computes the same mathematical product. No native implementation or build
was made. The spectral filter and word reuse remove most expensive
operations before this engineering choice is needed.

The next work should be a short proof review and an exact synthetic
finite-field construction of the six/eighteen tables, followed by a
separately identified proposer using lazy word prefixes and the trace
filter. Root can first retain the old positive power confirmation and the
literal direct verifier. Known old misses remain skipped and the same
old dictionary is not retried merely because its evaluator is faster.
Only genuinely unvisited unpaid cases enter any new Root-owned batch.
No wider conjecture search, intake expansion, case payment or canonical
state change is proposed by this note.

